1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
 What if I told you that watching a TV show with your kids, the thing that you feel a

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,360
 little guilty about, can help with sibling fights?

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:08,360
 Now stay with me.

4
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,040
 Be nice to your sister!

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,040
 We all say that.

6
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,500
 I've said it a million times too.

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,820
 And we all know it doesn't really work.

8
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:15,820
 And here's why.

9
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:18,880
 Your kid already has kindness inside them.

10
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:23,040
 When they're not being nice, something's blocking access to it.

11
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,040
 Jealousy.

12
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,040
 Anger.

13
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,440
 I didn't ask to be the responsible one.

14
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:30,880
 Whatever it is, think about it as a blocker to kindness.

15
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,280
 Be nice skips over all that.

16
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:34,920
 So no wonder it's not effective.

17
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:41,160
 And this is where the right TV show, yes TV, can actually be used as an effective tool.

18
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:45,560
 Because sometimes the hardest thing for a kid is to talk about this stuff head on.

19
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,920
 So we don't go head on.

20
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,640
 We do something we call a side door.

21
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,680
 And a show gives you the side door.

22
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:56,000
 In the new season of Gabby's Dollhouse, we meet Gabby's little sister, Doozy, for the

23
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
 first time.

24
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,160
 They're making frozen bananas, rolled in graham crackers, and coconut.

25
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,160
 Delicious.

26
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,160
 Having a blast.

27
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:07,320
 And when Doozy slams the door on her way out, Gabby just smiles and says, "I love my sister.

28
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:08,600
 Watch it together."

29
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:15,280
 And then afterward, in just low stakes kind of way, say something simple and short.

30
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:19,840
 Like hmm, sometimes a little sister can feel so good.

31
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,820
 And sometimes I bet it feels so hard.

32
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:25,480
 I bet Gabby feels mad at Doozy sometimes.

33
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,680
 That would make sense.

34
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,680
 Leave it at that.

35
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,080
 Now, here's what's key.

36
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:31,800
 Do not expect a profound reply.

37
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,600
 "Wow, Mom, just like me and my sibling.

38
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,600
 Won't happen.

39
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,600
 You're probably going to get silenced.

40
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,600
 Or can I have a snack?"

41
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,680
 Still, it landed.

42
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,680
 It matters.

43
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,880
 I promise.

44
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:44,180
 Now your kid knows it's okay to feel mad.

45
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:48,080
 Now your kid knows she can have love and frustration at a sibling at the same time, which means

46
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:55,000
 that frustration or mad feeling is less likely to come out as a hit or a tease or any less

47
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,960
 than ideal behavior all because you watched a TV episode and used it as a side

